1
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:06,631
[BEA] <i>Oliver? Oliver, right?</i>

2
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:08,383
<i>I'm Bea.</i>

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,263
<i>I'm your sister too.</i>

4
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,766
<i>If you want,</i>

5
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:19,102
<i>you can call me</i>

6
00:00:19,728 --> 00:00:21,020
<i>Big Sister Bea.</i>

7
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:22,647
[ENRICO] <i>I still can't believe</i>

8
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,442
<i>that we're together again.</i>

9
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,111
<i>Me neither.</i>

10
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:30,071
<i>Ah. By the way,</i>

11
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:32,782
<i>these are from Billy.</i>

12
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>- All of this?</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

13
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,619
<i>- For me?</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

14
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,622
<i>Take a look.</i>

15
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:42,208
<i>They're clothes.</i>

16
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,251
<i>Here.</i>

17
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:47,172
<i>- Billy gave me all these?</i>
<i>- Yes. And this too.</i>

18
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>So we can keep in touch with you.</i>

19
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:56,306
[STAMMERS]
<i>Please tell Billy I said thank you.</i>

20
00:00:56,389 --> 00:01:01,770
<i>It would have been enough that she</i>
<i>dropped the charges and forgave me.</i>

21
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,396
<i>This is too much.</i>

22
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:08,526
<i>P-please tell her that</i>
<i>I'm going to work hard.</i>

23
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:10,737
<i>I'm going to find a job.</i>

24
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>And I promise that I'm going to change.</i>

25
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,327
<i>Please tell Billy I'm going to change.</i>

26
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:22,874
<i>I'm already very happy.</i>

27
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:27,337
[PRISON GUARD] <i>The person</i>
<i>you're looking for isn't here.</i>

28
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:31,883
Carlos Toledo was one of the prisoners
who escaped last week.

29
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:33,885
<i>Escaped?</i>

30
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:47,774
[PHONE RINGING]

31
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:52,612
<i>Caloy?</i>

32
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:54,197
<i>Bea?</i>

33
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,490
<i>Caloy, where are you?</i>

34
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:56,658
<i>Let's meet.</i>

35
00:01:58,618 --> 00:01:59,911
<i>Bea.</i>

36
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:01,830
<i>Caloy.</i>

37
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:04,666
[CALOY] <i>How did you get out?</i>

38
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:06,709
<i>Billy forgave me.</i>

39
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,171
<i>Really?</i>

40
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,257
<i>How?</i>

41
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,175
<i>And why?</i>

42
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,472
<i>Billy and I are half-sisters.</i>

43
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:32,777
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:34,255
Y-You…

45
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:36,925
You should've told me sooner
that you were half-sisters.

46
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:40,303
Well…

47
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:44,432
I didn't want anyone else to find out.

48
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:47,227
It could've ruined my plan.

49
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,312
Well, it got ruined anyway.

50
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:51,981
You and your mother ended up in jail.

51
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,359
Well, I'm free now.

52
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:57,111
And I can finally carry out my plan.

53
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:59,197
You mean our plan.

54
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:01,032
We're in this together, right?

55
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:05,912
I won't let that half-sister of yours
bully you anymore.

56
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:07,872
I'll take both her and Jordan down.

57
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,457
Hey.

58
00:04:09,999 --> 00:04:11,501
- No.
- Calm down.

59
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:12,585
No.

60
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,878
Stop it, Caloy.

61
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,421
They're on high alert because of you.

62
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:18,716
If something bad happens
to Billy and her family,

63
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,135
I'm sure the blame will fall on me.

64
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:26,933
I can tell that Billy is still mad at me,

65
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,810
but guess what?

66
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:30,812
She gave me a cell phone,

67
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:36,401
clothes, and even cash.

68
00:04:36,901 --> 00:04:38,319
What happened?

69
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:40,738
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

70
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:43,950
After everything we worked for,
you gave in to bribes.

71
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,785
It's not like that.

72
00:04:45,868 --> 00:04:47,662
I'm just saying,

73
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:51,791
Billy's making an effort
to get along with me.

74
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:55,336
I know she's only doing it for our father.

75
00:04:55,962 --> 00:05:00,758
But at least she's trying, right?

76
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:02,593
Then let's go after Jordan.

77
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:04,429
Stop it, will you?

78
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:05,680
Calm down.

79
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:12,312
I found out Jordan's father
is your enemy now too.

80
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:14,230
So lie low for now.

81
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:16,399
We can't let the police catch you.

82
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:22,196
Because if Billy doesn't help me,

83
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:25,491
I'll need you to help me
break Mama out of jail.

84
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,492
[CALOY SCOFFS] Tch.

85
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:33,291
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:34,334
What's your problem?

87
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:35,418
Nothing.

88
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:37,170
Just tell me.

89
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:41,883
You only called me because you need me.

90
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:52,518
Come on…

91
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:55,521
You're right.

92
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:57,732
I need you.

93
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:01,360
Caloy…

94
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:04,363
Caloy, I need you.

95
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:06,741
And…

96
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:10,745
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,663
I love you.

98
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,671
Do you mean that?

99
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:26,135
You already know I do. Stop playing dumb.

100
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,473
You see, Caloy,

101
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:33,851
Mama wants a complete family.

102
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:36,938
And I'll give her that.

103
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,358
She wants

104
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:43,194
to take Papa back.

105
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,988
She wants our family back together.

106
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:48,991
When that happens…

107
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,829
you'll be part of that family.

108
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:59,752
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

109
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:06,801
How about you?

110
00:07:07,718 --> 00:07:09,053
Is that what you want too?

111
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:12,223
For your father to come back to you?

112
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:29,991
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

113
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:53,639
[MUSIC FADES]

114
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:58,644
I've sent you the list of investors
who might reconsider.

115
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,023
Try to set a meeting with them.

116
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:05,193
I also sent the pitch deck through email.

117
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,320
Copy, chief.

118
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:13,951
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:15,995
I'm sorry, Billy.

120
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:19,916
You had to handle everything on your own.

121
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:25,254
I know there's so much going
on in your life right now,

122
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,840
and yet you're still hanging in there.

123
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:34,305
Promise. From now on, we will do better.

124
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:36,682
No.

125
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,854
I'm the one who needs to
apologize to you all.

126
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,233
I'm sorry.

127
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:48,945
Sometimes, I end up
taking my anger out on you.

128
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:54,408
It's okay, we understand.

129
00:08:56,285 --> 00:08:58,412
So, how are things
between you and your sister?

130
00:09:00,998 --> 00:09:02,792
I wouldn't call her that.

131
00:09:05,169 --> 00:09:09,382
Does that mean even though
you dropped the charges,

132
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:11,050
you're still wary of her?

133
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,470
I learned from my experience.

134
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:21,227
- Um, anyway, check my email.
- Oh, yes.

135
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:22,979
I made some revisions on page 7.

136
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:24,939
- Mm-hmm. Okay.
- Just check it.

137
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:27,900
Also, kindly double-check…

138
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:30,611
- Um, Toni, please--
- Billy, can we talk?

139
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,071
Sorry, dude.

140
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:34,115
We're still discussing something.

141
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:35,074
[JORDAN] Uh…

142
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:36,951
Dude, this is important.

143
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:41,330
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:42,331
Okay.

145
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,922
- Aah!
- Hey!

146
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,593
- You can scream here.
- No, you can't!

147
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:55,595
[BOTH CHUCKLE SOFTLY]

148
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:59,473
If my gigs can't take your stress away,

149
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,434
then this might help.

150
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:03,394
- Come on, give it a try.
- I don't think so. [CHUCKLES]

151
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:04,478
Let's do it together.

152
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:06,606
No!

153
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:07,898
Don't do it!

154
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:10,109
[BOTH CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

155
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:11,193
There.

156
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,821
I'm just happy that…

157
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:18,326
I made you feel a bit lighter.

158
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:20,244
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:10:20,828 --> 00:10:24,206
I'm sorry that I haven't been able
to catch your gigs lately.

160
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,250
I'm sorry, too,

161
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:29,253
that we don't get to celebrate your wins.

162
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,213
I'm such a terrible best friend.

163
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:33,132
You've always been there for me,

164
00:10:33,215 --> 00:10:34,967
but I let you down.

165
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:38,137
Even if you don't say a word, I get you.

166
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:41,098
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,100
But still, thank you for the apology

168
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,310
because…

169
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:47,813
you've been kind of rude lately, you know?

170
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:51,901
I know.

171
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:55,321
I'm sorry again.

172
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:01,994
Thank you for still being here.

173
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:09,960
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:19,303
Come on, tell me. What is it?

175
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:21,972
Uh…

176
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:24,642
Okay.

177
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:30,314
Dad came to visit me.

178
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:32,525
[MUSIC BECOMES UNEASY]

179
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:34,110
He apologized to me.

180
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:39,990
It turns out he was in jail all this time.

181
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:46,747
So he was released from jail?

182
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:48,749
No.

183
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:52,795
He broke out

184
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,338
with Caloy.

185
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:57,383
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:11:57,466 --> 00:11:58,676
What?!

187
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:07,518
Dude, I'm sorry.
I've known this for a couple of days.

188
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:10,146
Seriously, Jordan?!

189
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:12,940
I didn't want to tell you

190
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:15,734
because I didn't want to add
to your problems.

191
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:19,071
Not telling me would only
make things worse.

192
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:23,242
You know that Caloy is a dangerous man.

193
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:27,788
What else?

194
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,915
What else are you not telling me?

195
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:32,710
Uh, last week,

196
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:35,588
he tried to hit me with a car.

197
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:38,299
- What?!
- Billy, relax.

198
00:12:38,382 --> 00:12:40,301
- Oh my God!
- I'm okay.

199
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:42,636
Fortunately, my dad was there.

200
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,139
He… He saved me.

201
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:48,767
Look, Billy.

202
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:53,939
When my dad came to me
and apologized to me,

203
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:55,858
I tried to make a deal with him.

204
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,946
I told him I'd forgive him

205
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,948
if he helped me catch Caloy.

206
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:06,035
And we almost did.

207
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:10,080
But Caloy, he pulled a gun.

208
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:11,582
He tried to shoot me,

209
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:14,418
and Dad blocked him and got shot.

210
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:17,338
Why are you only
telling me this now, Jordan?!

211
00:13:17,421 --> 00:13:18,589
Why?!

212
00:13:18,672 --> 00:13:22,218
Because I wanted Caloy
to be back in jail before I told you.

213
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:25,221
But you didn't catch him,
and you almost died again.

214
00:13:25,304 --> 00:13:26,764
But I didn't die.

215
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:29,350
Because of him.

216
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:33,187
Jordan.

217
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:36,148
Even though your dad saved you,

218
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:38,734
you need to report him to the police.

219
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,654
Even if he's sorry for what he did,

220
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:44,698
he's still a criminal.

221
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:51,288
And hiding him
will also get you in trouble.

222
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:56,961
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:59,046
Well, Jordan?

224
00:13:59,129 --> 00:14:01,006
Are you going to tell me?

225
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:05,636
Do you know where your father is hiding?

226
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:11,225
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

227
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:18,607
When I saw how you and your father
patched things up,

228
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,652
and how you were happy together,

229
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:24,947
I thought to myself, "What if?"

230
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:28,158
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:32,788
What if my father and I
also patched things up?

232
00:14:34,331 --> 00:14:36,041
He told me

233
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:38,836
he wants to start a new life.

234
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:42,256
Jordan.

235
00:14:43,883 --> 00:14:47,303
My father was imprisoned in Canada

236
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:50,014
and served his sentence.

237
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:53,142
Your father escaped from jail.
It's not the same.

238
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:58,814
No matter how you look at it,
that's illegal.

239
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,524
He's a criminal.

240
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:05,696
He needs to go back to jail.

241
00:15:06,697 --> 00:15:09,658
Bea also committed crimes,
but you had her acquitted.

242
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:14,204
I'm sorry.

243
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,791
Billy, I'm sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

244
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:19,752
Especially about Caloy.

245
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,298
I got a little complacent

246
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:28,510
because I made arrangements
with the police.

247
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:31,347
I asked them to guard you.

248
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:38,103
At your apartment, at work,
or wherever else you go.

249
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:41,607
- [BILLY HUFFS]
- Look, I…

250
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:45,235
Billy, I also want to apologize because…

251
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:48,948
I want to forgive my dad.

252
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:50,574
Yes, I get your point.

253
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:54,370
His case is different from your father's.

254
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:57,831
But the thing is, he's still my father.

255
00:15:57,915 --> 00:16:02,711
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

256
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:05,255
Despite what he did in the past…

257
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:13,097
I feel like I can forgive him.

258
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:21,271
I just want to give him a chance
at least to start over.

259
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:28,070
[UPLIFTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

260
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,211
[MUSIC STOPS]

261
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:46,422
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

262
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:57,641
Miss, I'm here to visit Mariela Mercado.

263
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:00,853
She's in Room 202.

264
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:04,440
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:06,525
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

266
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:13,449
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:19,913
Aren't you tired of just standing there?!

268
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:21,248
Get out!

269
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:22,458
- Leave!
- Ma!

270
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:24,668
Ma! Ma…

271
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:27,296
- What are you doing?
- [MARIELA SOBS]

272
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,256
Sorry about that.

273
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:32,092
[MARIELA SOBBING, SNIFFLING]

274
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:34,553
- Ma…
- Why did you only visit me now?

275
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:36,096
Look! [SNIFFLES]

276
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:39,391
This is what they're doing to me!
They're hurting me!

277
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:41,143
Ma'am, that's not true.

278
00:17:41,226 --> 00:17:43,020
She was extremely distressed
the other night.

279
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:46,148
She wouldn't calm down
and ended up hurting herself.

280
00:17:46,231 --> 00:17:47,733
- That's your fault!
- Ma.

281
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:49,401
Enough.

282
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:51,236
Shh.

283
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,530
- Uh, ma'am?
- [MARIELA SNIFFLING]

284
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:56,408
Miss, could you give us some privacy?

285
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:59,078
I'd like to talk to my mom alone.

286
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:01,371
- Okay.
- Thank you.

287
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:08,087
- [MARIELA SNIFFLING]
- Ma…

288
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:12,091
Ma, what did I tell you?

289
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:15,761
Didn't I tell you to behave here?

290
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,055
Endure it a little longer.

291
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:20,390
I'll get you out of here soon, okay?

292
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:21,892
When exactly?

293
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:23,560
Bea…

294
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:27,815
Take me with you. I hate it here.

295
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:33,737
How can we be a complete family
with your dad if I'm stuck here?

296
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:37,199
We should be together, not them.

297
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,577
No matter what they say,

298
00:18:40,661 --> 00:18:43,247
that woman your father's with
is still his mistress.

299
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:46,834
And you're playing nice with his bastards
from his other mistress.

300
00:18:46,917 --> 00:18:49,044
They're painting us as the bad guys?

301
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:53,715
Since when did it become acceptable
to be a mistress

302
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:56,844
and have illegitimate children
with a married man?

303
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:58,137
Since when?

304
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:03,767
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:19:12,943 --> 00:19:15,320
<i>Have some more, Oliver. Here.</i>

306
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:18,115
<i>He can't. We're monitoring Oliver's diet.</i>

307
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:19,283
<i>He has diabetes.</i>

308
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:20,576
<i>Eat up.</i>

309
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:21,952
<i>Oh, right.</i>

310
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:24,621
<i>- You have it, Pa.</i>
<i>- He's diabetic too.</i>

311
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:27,291
<i>We're limiting his consumption of meat.</i>

312
00:19:29,334 --> 00:19:31,170
<i>You can have it.</i>

313
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:34,339
[CHUCKLES] <i>Then I'll help myself.</i>

314
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:38,844
<i>I love Auntie Precious's cooking.</i>

315
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:41,054
<i>- It's delicious.</i>
<i>- Thank you.</i>

316
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:46,476
<i>I know adobo is your favorite.</i>

317
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:51,023
<i>You remember?</i>

318
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:55,777
<i>It's Mama's specialty after all.</i>

319
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:59,406
<i>Things are finally looking better</i>
<i>for my family now.</i>

320
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:03,118
<i>They almost died because of the fire.</i>

321
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:06,121
<i>The fire that your mother started.</i>

322
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:12,586
<i>So you understand why</i>
<i>she can't be absolved, right?</i>

323
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,340
<i>Now, about Caloy…</i>

324
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:20,802
<i>Do you know he escaped?</i>

325
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:27,309
<i>You didn't know?</i>

326
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:29,311
<i>Huh?</i>

327
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:32,105
<i>You're no longer in touch?</i>

328
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:34,816
<i>N-N… No!</i>

329
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:38,278
[SCOFFS] <i>Billy,</i>
<i>how would we get in touch?</i>

330
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,989
<i>I don't have his number.</i>

331
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:43,825
<i>We're… We're not…</i>
<i>We're not together, remember?</i>

332
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:46,495
<i>But I hope he does contact me.</i>

333
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:48,455
<i>What?</i>

334
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:56,421
<i>You know,</i>

335
00:20:57,923 --> 00:21:02,761
<i>I heard Grandpa and Mom's</i>
<i>conversation back then.</i>

336
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:10,811
<i>Grandpa was urging her to leave you.</i>

337
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:15,357
<i>Because as well as physically hurting her,</i>

338
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:18,944
<i>you also had the gall to cheat on her.</i>

339
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,908
<i>It's okay. Be honest with me.</i>

340
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:26,618
<i>Who's your mistress?</i>

341
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:28,787
<i>Karen?</i>

342
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:31,540
[CLEARS THROAT]

343
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:36,503
<i>You didn't respect Mom.</i>

344
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:41,883
<i>You even gave her necklace</i>
<i>to your mistress.</i>

345
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:44,052
[SIGHS] <i>You know,</i>

346
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:48,682
<i>you're so stingy for someone</i>
<i>who earns so much.</i>

347
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:54,146
<i>I owe you nothing.</i>

348
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:56,106
<i>Well, think again, hmm?</i>

349
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:59,735
<i>That song that made you famous?</i>

350
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:02,487
<i>Who do you think</i>
<i>your mother wrote that for?</i>

351
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:04,448
<i>For you? No.</i>

352
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:07,534
<i>She wrote it for the two of us.</i>

353
00:22:07,617 --> 00:22:13,915
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
